## PORT DESIGN

Core is SDL/desktop+Win32 only via these modules. We REPLACE them with Android
implementations exposing the SAME symbol names, and EXCLUDE the SDL/Win32 .c.

CORE EDITS (DONE in T03) - guarded so desktop still builds:
- config.h      : `#define USE_NE2000` wrapped in `#ifndef __ANDROID__` (NE2000
                  needs <pcap.h> which NDK lacks). ENABLE_TCP_MODEM already
                  _WIN32-only. USE_DISK_HLE stays ON (HLE disk needs no pcap).
- sdlconsole.h  : removed `#include <SDL.h>` block; sig changed to
                  `uint8_t sdlconsole_translateScancode(int keyval);`
- sdlconsole.c  : matched `int keyval` (desktop SDL impl untouched otherwise).
- sdlaudio.h    : removed `#include <SDL.h>` block.
machine.c is ALREADY guarded (#ifdef USE_NE2000 / #ifdef ENABLE_TCP_MODEM around
all ne2000/pcap/tcpmodem calls) -> no edit. pcap-win32.c, ne2000.c, tcpmodem.c,
menus.c, main.c are EXCLUDED from the NDK source list (see Android.mk).

