## SYMBOL CONTRACT (what each NEW native file provides/defines)

### jni/android_frontend.h  +  jni/android_frontend.c  (TASK T05)
Implements the sdlconsole_* symbols expected by cga.c/vga.c (now SDL-free header),
plus Android-only helpers used by jni_bridge.c. Video render thread (cga/vga) calls
sdlconsole_blit from a native thread -> framebuffer copy is mutex-protected.

Public (declared in android_frontend.h, used by jni_bridge.c):
  void android_fb_get_dims(int *w, int *h);        // current framebuffer size
  int  android_fb_copy(int32_t *out, int count);   // copy min(count, w*h) pixels; pixel=0xFFRRGGBB; returns copied
  uint8_t android_keycode_to_scancode(int keycode); // Android KEYCODE -> PC XT set-1 MAKE code

Implements (declared in sdlconsole.h, defined here - so link succeeds):
  int  sdlconsole_init(char *title);            // alloc 1024x1024 RGB fb + mutex; return 0
  void sdlconsole_blit(uint32_t* pixels,int w,int h,int stride); // stride in BYTES; copy w*h
  int  sdlconsole_loop(void);                    // return SDLCONSOLE_EVENT_NONE (events via JNI callbacks)
  uint8_t sdlconsole_getScancode(void);         // last scancode set by key injection
  uint8_t sdlconsole_translateScancode(int keyval); // == android_keycode_to_scancode
  int  sdlconsole_setWindow(int w,int h);       // no-op, return 0
  void sdlconsole_setTitle(char* title);        // no-op

android_keycode_to_scancode table (PC XT set-1 MAKE codes). Android codes from
KeyEvent.java (A=29..Z=54, 0..9=7..16, ENTER=66, DEL=67, TAB=61, SPACE=62,
COMMA=55, PERIOD=56, MINUS=69, EQUALS=70, GRAVE=68, SEMICOLON=74, APOSTROPHE=75,
SLASH=76, BACKSLASH=73, LEFT_BRACKET=71, RIGHT_BRACKET=72, ESC=111, CAPS_LOCK=115,
DPAD_UP=19,DPAD_DOWN=20,DPAD_LEFT=21,DPAD_RIGHT=22, SHIFT_LEFT=59, SHIFT_RIGHT=60,
ALT_LEFT=57, ALT_RIGHT=58, F1=131..F12=142). Map:
  Esc 111->01 | ` 68->29 | 1(7)->02 2(8)->03 3(9)->04 4(10)->05 5(11)->06
  6(13)->07 7(14)->08 8(15)->09 9(16)->0A 0(7)->0B | -(69)->0C =(70)->0D
  Backspace 67->0E | Tab 61->0F
  Q(45)->10 W(51)->11 E(33)->12 R(46)->13 T(48)->14 Y(53)->15 U(49)->16
  I(37)->17 O(43)->18 P(44)->19 | [(71)->1A ](72)->1B Enter(66)->1C
  LCtrl: use KEYCODE_CTRL_LEFT if present ->1D (else treat LAlt/RCtrl via ext)
  A(29)->1E S(47)->1F D(32)->20 F(34)->21 G(35)->22 H(36)->23 J(38)->24
  K(39)->25 L(40)->26 | ;(74)->27 '(75)->28
  LShift(59)->2A | \(73)->2B
  Z(54)->2C X(52)->2D C(31)->2E V(50)->2F B(30)->30 N(42)->31 M(41)->32
  ,(55)->33 .(56)->34 /(76)->35 | RShift(60)->36
  LAlt(57)->38 | Space(62)->39 | CapsLock(115)->3A | F1(131)->3B..F10(140)->44
  F11(141)->57 F12(142)->58
  DPAD Up(19)->48 Down(20)->50 Left(21)->4B Right(22)->4D
  Unknown keycode -> return 0 (ignored, no IRQ).
Notes: don't map RAlt/RCtrl distinctly (set-1 extended handling is complex); treat
ALT_LEFT as 0x38 and that's enough for Alt-combos in DOS.

### jni/android_audio.c  (TASK T06)
Implements sdlaudio_* (declared in sdlaudio.h) via OpenSL ES. The timer callback
sdlaudio_generateSample (registered in sdlaudio_init) mixes pcspeaker/OPL3/blaster
and calls sdlaudio_bufferSample to feed a ring buffer; an OpenSL buffer-queue
callback drains it to the device (48000 Hz, mono, S16LE).
  int  sdlaudio_init(MACHINE_t* machine);        // create OB+buffer queue; return 0
  void sdlaudio_generateSample(void* dummy);     // unchanged mixer logic
  void sdlaudio_updateSampleTiming(void);        // unchanged timing adjust; resume OB on NORMAL
  void sdlaudio_bufferSample(int16_t val);       // push to ring buffer (mutex)
If OpenSL init fails: return 0, leave audio silent (generateSample still fills buffer,
drain callback a no-op). Link errors to avoid: do NOT reference SDL_* symbols; do NOT
include <SDL.h>. Use #include <SLES/OpenSLES.h> <SLES/OpenSLES_Android.h> + pthread.
Ring buffer size SAMPLE_BUFFER (4800). Keep SAMPLE_RATE (48000) from config.h.
Thread-safety: generateSample runs on the timing/nativeRun thread; OB callback runs on
the OpenSL thread -> protect ring buffer indices with a pthread_mutex.

### jni/jni_bridge.c  (TASK T07)  [name matches Android.mk source list]
Defines (because main.c is EXCLUDED, its globals must be provided here):
  volatile uint8_t running = 1;
  uint8_t videocard = 0xFF, showMIPS = 0;
  double speed = 0;            // config.h extern double speed (non-volatile)
  uint32_t baudrate = 115200, ramsize = 640;  // config.h extern
  char* usemachine = "generic_xt";           // config.h extern
  uint8_t bootdrive;                         // config.h extern
(Private run-loop state, file-scope static: goCPU, limitCPU, instructionsperloop,
 cpuLimitTimer, ops, the optimer/cputimer callbacks, pending-key state, pause flag.)
Implements the 9 JNI methods from jni/xtulator_jni.h (package com.xtulator.android,
class XTulatorActivity -> Java_com_xtulator_android_XTulatorActivity_native*):
  nativeInit(biosPath,diskPath)->int:
    chdir(dirname(biosPath)) so roms/ tree resolves;
    ports_init(); timing_init(); memory_init();
    sdlconsole_init(title); sdlaudio_init(&machine);
    machine.pcap_if=-1; machine_init(&machine, usemachine);
    if videocard==0xFF set to VGA; if diskPath: biosdisk_insert(&machine.CPU,2,
    diskPath); bootdrive=0x80; biosdisk_init(&machine.CPU);  [see notes]
    timing_addTimer(optimer,NULL,10,ON); cpuLimitTimer=add(cputimer,...,10000);
    return 0 (negative on init failure).
  nativeRun(): while(running){ if paused: sleep 10ms+continue;
    if limitCPU==0 goCPU=1; if goCPU: drain pending key (scancode, isNew, IRQ1);
    cpu_interruptCheck(&machine.CPU,&machine.i8259); cpu_exec(&machine.CPU,N);
    timing_loop(); sdlaudio_updateSampleTiming(); sleep 1ms when !goCPU to idle; }
  nativeStop(): running=0. nativePause(): pause flag=1. nativeResume(): pause=0.
  nativeResize(w,h): store surface dims (for Java scaling).
  nativeKeyDown(k): sc=android_keycode_to_scancode(k); if sc: set pending key sc
    (make, isNew=1) -> run loop injects. Also handle modifiers (Shift/Ctrl/Alt) by
    setting a shift state consumed in injection (set KeyState + IRQ1).
  nativeKeyUp(k): sc = android_keycode_to_scancode(k); if sc: pending = sc|0x80 (break).
  nativeMouseEvent(action,x,y): call mouse_action(MOUSE_ACTION_MOVE/MOUSE_*, ...).
  nativeGetFbWidth/Height -> int (query android_fb_get_dims) [EXTRA, Java declares].
  nativeCopyFrame(jintArray out): android_fb_copy on GetElements->Release, return copied.
Thread note: nativeInit runs on UI thread (onCreate) and spawns cga/vga render threads;
nativeRun runs on a Java Thread (mEmulatorThread). Framebuffer+ringbuf are mutex-safe.
Includes (use ../XTulator/ paths): ../XTulator/config.h, machine.h, cpu/cpu.h,
chipset/i8259.h, modules/disk/biosdisk.h, modules/video/sdlconsole.h,
modules/audio/sdlaudio.h, timing.h, debuglog.h, modules/input/mouse.h,
<jni.h>, <android/log.h>, "android_frontend.h". <stdio.h> for chdir(dirname).

### android/src/.../XTulatorActivity.java  (TASK T08)
Keep native method names. Add:
  - assetExtract(): copy assets/roms/** -> filesDir/roms (if not exist) and
    assets/disk.img -> filesDir/disk.img (if not exist). Graceful if absent.
  - nativeInit(getFilesDir().absPath, filesDir+"/disk.img") [chdir to filesDir so
    roms/ tree resolves; disk inserted via biosdisk_insert].
  - Replace XTulatorView to: hold Bitmap (ARGB_8888) sized to nativeGetFb{W,H};
    30fps Handler loop: nativeCopyFrame(pixels[]) -> Bitmap.setPixels -> invalidate;
    onDraw: canvas.drawBitmap(mBitmap, null, dstRect, null) (scale fb to view).
  - onKeyDown/onKeyUp -> nativeKeyDown/nativeKeyUp. onTrackballEvent / onTouchEvent ->
    nativeMouseEvent(MOUSE_ACTION_MOVE, x, y) (trackball = mouse move). Landscape fixed.
  - native GetFbWidth/Height declared native. Keep System.loadLibrary("xtulator").

ASSETS REQUIRED (user supplies in Docker context):
  android/assets/roms/machine/generic_xt/pcxtbios.bin   (16KB, generic_xt BIOS)
  android/assets/roms/video/et4000.bin                  (32KB, VGA BIOS)
  android/assets/disk.img                               (FreeDOS/any disk)
Without roms, machine_init fails -> nativeInit returns <0. (Not a code bug.)

